{"base_rate":0.5275590551181102,"brier":0.1904566929133858,"bss":0.23585174129353248,"bss_hi":0.3404024292160833,"bss_lo":0.1320612469467513,"country":"FR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16136482939632543,"ess":418.59206261883435,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Paris</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Paris rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>97%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>22%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nORLY, 15.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.24, ranked 83 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(50&ndash;99) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>304</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>97%</b></td><td class='num'>153</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Paris</b> <span class=\"muted\">FR</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.24</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>50&ndash;99\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Paris &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Paris\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.572039473684214,377.2105263157895 86.52823529411765,328.47058823529414 149.13341463414633,253.26829268292684 245.03000000000003,149.44444444444446 340.6028915662651,61.855421686747036 403.2078431372549,20.37908496732024 403.2078431372549,37.03267973856208 340.6028915662651,123.25301204819277 245.03000000000003,230.33333333333331 149.13341463414633,319.8536585365854 86.52823529411765,376.6470588235294 59.572039473684214,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"189.96850393700788\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"189.96850393700788\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.572039473684214,301.7763157894737 86.52823529411765,258.88235294117646 149.13341463414633,195.5609756097561 245.03000000000003,109.0 340.6028915662651,83.7831325301205 403.2078431372549,29.895424836601308\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 304 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.572039473684214\" cy=\"301.7763157894737\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"86.52823529411765\" cy=\"258.88235294117646\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 26%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"149.13341463414633\" cy=\"195.5609756097561\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 53%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"245.03000000000003\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"340.6028915662651\" cy=\"83.7831325301205\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 97% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 153 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"403.2078431372549\" cy=\"29.895424836601308\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(53%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Paris the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.35) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.21).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'>-0.213</td><td class='num'>27.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.270</td><td class='num'>11.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>0.339</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.354</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":48.85341,"lon":2.3488,"n":762,"n_cities":109,"name":"Paris","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0044407894736842105,"n":304,"obs":0.22039473684210525,"sig":true},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.08058823529411764,"n":68,"obs":0.3382352941176471,"sig":true},{"hi":0.4,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.25743902439024385,"n":82,"obs":0.5121951219512195,"sig":true},{"hi":0.68,"lo":0.4,"mean":0.5283333333333334,"n":72,"obs":0.75,"sig":true},{"hi":0.8960000000000014,"lo":0.68,"mean":0.7983132530120483,"n":83,"obs":0.8192771084337349,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.8960000000000014,"mean":0.9751633986928104,"n":153,"obs":0.9673202614379085,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":15.3,"rank":83,"rank_hi":99.02499999999998,"rank_lo":50.0,"reliability":0.036216400087288034,"resolution":0.09363983748543606,"slug":"paris","station":"ORLY","timezone":"Europe/Paris"}